    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5ac95200",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: the_look_on_your_face_after_killing_someone; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in a suit with a smug or self-satisfied expression, overlaid with text that reads 'the look on your face after killing someone!'. This juxtaposition is intended to be shocking and provocative, using a well-known meme format to imply that the person depicted is guilty of a serious crime. The meme's intent is to elicit strong emotional reactions (shock, disgust, outrage) from viewers by associating the subject with extreme violence. While it does not target any specific protected group, it is harmful because it promotes a violent and morally reprehensible act, potentially normalizing or trivializing murder. The meme is not abusive or cyberbullying in the traditional sense, but it is harmful as it encourages viewers to imagine or associate the subject with a horrific crime, which can be psychologically disturbing and may contribute to a culture that glorifies or sensationalizes violence. The intent is to shock and provoke, using the visual of a calm, composed individual to contrast with the violent crime described in the text, thereby creating a jarring and unsettling effect.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_efd490d3"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
